      "title": "README - Keyframe Chain",
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Keyframe Chain - MiniMax FastH3\n**Geekatplay Studio - Vladimir Chopine**\nhttps://www.geekatplay.com\n\n### The chain\nEach image is the **closing** frame of one segment and the **opening** frame of the next:\n\n| segment | first frame | last frame |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | image 1 | image 2 |\n| 2 | image 2 | image 3 |\n| 3 | image 3 | image 4 |\n| 4 | image 4 | *none - tail* |\n\nThe tail segment is image-to-video with no closing frame, so the movie does not end on a\nfreeze. Turn `tail_segment` off on the manager if you want it to stop on the last image.\n\n### The prompt is FORMATTED, not written\n`prompt_mode` defaults to **format my text only (no AI, no invention)**. It rewrites what you\ntype into MiniMax H3 motion grammar and adds nothing - no model is called, so it cannot\nhallucinate:\n\nYour sentence is split into a scene part and a camera part. The scene part is kept\n**word for word**; only the camera part is restated in the documented grammar.\n\n| you type | it sends |\n|---|---|\n| `the girl dancing in the enchanted forest and camera orbiting around her` | `[Shot 1] the girl dancing in the enchanted forest. The camera orbits with medium amplitude at medium speed.` |\n| `slow pan right` | `[Shot 1] The camera pans right with medium amplitude at slow speed.` |\n| `wide shot of mountains at dawn` | `[Shot 1] wide shot of mountains at dawn.` |\n| `hold still` | `[Shot 1] The camera holds static.` |\n\nNothing is dropped and nothing is added. If no camera wording is recognised the sentence\npasses through untouched. `prompt_preview` reports exactly what was done.\n\n`style_mode` on the manager defaults to **none - send only my prompt**, so no look\ninstruction is appended either. `closing_frame_note` is off for the same reason.\n\nThe other modes: **format with Ollama (strict)** uses the LLM but throws its answer away if\nit introduces any word you never wrote; **expand creatively** lets it write freely.\n\n### IMPORTANT: describe motion, not content\nThis is image-to-video. Your pictures already decide what is in frame, how it is framed and\nwhat it looks like. The description on each Keyframe Input should say only how things MOVE.\n\nDo not write a shot size (\"medium shot\", \"over-the-shoulder\") and do not write \"the subject\" -\nan over-the-shoulder shot means a shot of a person, so asking for one over a landscape makes\nthe model invent a person.\n\n`style_mode` on the manager defaults to **follow the supplied frames**, which tells the model\nto keep your images' look and add nothing. Use `full style lock` only when you deliberately\nwant the render to depart from the source frames.\n\n### Seeing what the AI wrote\nEvery Segment Generator's **`prompt_preview`** goes to its own preview node, and the manager's\n**`segment_prompts`** shows the FINAL text sent to MiniMax H3 for each segment - including\nwhich keyframe was anchored as the first frame, which as the last, and at what frame index.\n\n### Adding or removing keyframes\nThe Segment Manager grows its own inputs. Fill `segment_4` and a `segment_5` slot appears;\ndisconnect one and the empty slot goes away. Up to 12. Order matters - slot order **is**\nstory order.\n\nTo add a keyframe: copy a LoadImage + Keyframe Input + Segment Generator group, and drop its\n`segment` output onto the manager's empty slot.\n"
      ]
    },
