      "title": "Segment length, style & music",
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Segment length\n\nEach **Segment Generator** reads its description and picks **3s to 10s** on its own:\n\n- a held portrait scores low and lands near 3s\n- running, leaping, transforming, several beats in one sentence, or a spoken line all push\n  it up toward 10s\n\nOverride it three ways, in order of priority:\n\n1. `duration_override` on a **Keyframe Input** (0 = off) - that one segment only\n2. `duration_mode: fixed` on a **Segment Generator** - that one segment\n3. `duration_source` on the **Segment Manager** - all segments at once\n   (`manager override` forces its value, `clamp` only shortens)\n\nEvery length is snapped to MiniMax H3's 17k+5 frame grid at 24 fps, so 5.0s becomes 5.17s\n(124 frames). The generator reports what it picked on its `prompt_preview` output.\n\n## Screen shape and screen size\n`aspect_ratio` sets the SHAPE (`match first keyframe` copies the first image's proportions).\n`frame_size` sets the SIZE - how many pixels that shape is rendered at:\n\n| frame_size | 16:9 | 9:16 |\n|---|---|---|\n| auto / 1344 | 1344x768 | 768x1344 |\n| 1024 long edge | 1024x576 | 576x1024 |\n| 768 long edge | 768x448 | 448x768 |\n| 640 long edge | 640x352 | 352x640 |\n\nSmaller is much faster to render. Both axes snap to 32 and the area is capped to what\nMiniMax H3 supports, so no combination can produce an invalid canvas.\n\n## Style lives on the manager\nThe generators write only what MOVES. The manager stamps the same style, mood and video-type\nclause onto every segment, so the look cannot drift between shots.\n\n## Music\n`LoadAudio` is bypassed (ctrl+B). Un-bypass it to add a bed, then pick a `music_mix_mode`.\n\n## Lipsync (experimental)\nConnect speech to `lipsync_audio_0`, `lipsync_audio_1`... to drive the matching segment.\nSee the README before relying on it.\n"
      ]
    },
